  "response_text": "The __io_putchar function is meant to send a single character to the uart2 I/O channel. The function then returns this letter so that the printf function can output them as a string to the output channel. The __io_putchar function specifically allows the programmer to select which output is used, if this was part of a standard library than the programmer wouldn\u2019t be able to do this. This allows the programmer to better test that certain features are being used correctly.\\n",
